From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unidrv: colour lasers' raster -- Lexmark's universal driver prints its pages

Lexmark's Universal v2 driver is a GPD on Unidrv (*Personality HPGL2,
24-bit colour) with a render plug-in that hooks only DrvBitBlt and
passes the drawing back to the core. Its pages came out empty:

- A plug-in that hooks DrvBitBlt but not DrvCopyBits never saw the page:
  the copy now goes to its DrvBitBlt, as the hooks it asked for say.
- With a vector personality we sent no raster at all; but a plug-in that
  passes the drawing back to the core means the core draws the page, so
  the page (or band) is sent as raster after all.
- The GPD's raster commands (CmdSetSrcBmpWidth, CmdBeginRaster,
  CmdSendBlockData, CmdEndRaster) are its resolutions' option commands:
  a command is now looked for in the selected options too.
- Raster for such a printer is sent as the GPD's raster groups: the
  width, a block of rows compressed as TIFF 4.0 (PackBits) when the GPD
  has CmdEnableTIFF4, the end; 24-bit device colour is RGB, not BGR.
  The PCL XL raster block (1022) is only for *Personality PCLXL.

Lexmark's universal driver now prints PCL with HP-GL/2 and raster that
renders as the page.

Test: test/unidrvrast-gate.sh with test/unidrvgl-plugin.c, our own GPD
and plug-in (mutants SG_MUTANT_OPTIONCMD, RASTERGROUP, BLTHOOK,
COREDRAWN, RGB24).
